					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-625542#post-1819898</guid>
				<title>Re: REVELATION</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-625542/history-of-the-universe:part-one#post-1819898</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jul 2013 19:08:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>toadking07</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1632267</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Wow! Crazy! Good detective skills, nice find! Will the interview be added to this page<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-352320-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> or to a new one altogether?</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-352320-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/history-of-the-universe-part-one">http://www.scp-wiki.net/history-of-the-universe-part-one</a></div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-625542#post-1819895</guid>
				<title>Re: REVELATION</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-625542/history-of-the-universe:part-one#post-1819895</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jul 2013 19:02:14 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Salman Corbette</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>678987</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>But it's different, man. He wanted to escape the life of fame and glamour, to live among the common folk, anonymous and unknown. He was the leader SCP deserved, but not the one it needed. SCP needed a new hero, one who was not enshrouded in the clouds of mystery and the tales of legend, a perfect entity so lost to reality that his ideal kept people going in spite of it all, and his true nature would only disillusion the masses to the true aimlessness of their existence. Indeed, this man has performed the greatest of services, by performing no services at all.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
